00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:11.480 align:start position:0%
Cuba's former revolutionary leader Fidel  Castro has died he was 90 years old his  brother and successor President Raul  Castro announced his death on Cuban  state television Friday evening Fidel  was best known as a communist dictator  and remained at odds with the United  States of America many Cubans world  leaders and celebs across the nation  reacted to the news on Saturday  president-elect Donald Trump released a  statement that read today the world  marks the passing of a brutal dictator  who oppressed his own people for nearly  six decades President Obama offered  condolences to Fidel's family and wrote  the Cuban people must know that they  have a friend and partner in the United  States of America Cuban American  musician Emilio Estefan pinned an  emotional message to those who died  under Castro's regime writing we thank  you and honor you for fighting for  freedom and human rights for our  homeland your sacrifice will never be  forgotten  today there is a new dawn filled with  hope for our beloved Cuba his wife  Gloria shared the same sentiments  writing on Instagram although the death  of a human being is rarely cause for  celebration  it is the symbolic death of the  destructive ideologies that he espoused  that I believe is filling the Cuban  exile community with renewed hope and a  relief that has been long in coming
 

